Write a solution to find the people who have the most friends and the most friends number.

The test cases are generated so that only one person has the most friends.

The result format is in the following example.

 

Example 1:

Input: 
RequestAccepted table:
+--------------+-------------+-------------+
| requester_id | accepter_id | accept_date |
+--------------+-------------+-------------+
| 1            | 2           | 2016/06/03  |
| 1            | 3           | 2016/06/08  |
| 2            | 3           | 2016/06/08  |
| 3            | 4           | 2016/06/09  |
+--------------+-------------+-------------+
Output: 
+----+-----+
| id | num |
+----+-----+
| 3  | 3   |
+----+-----+

with base as(select requester_id id from RequestAccepted
union all
select accepter_id id from RequestAccepted)


select id, count(*) num  from base group by 1 order by 2 desc limit 1

--------------------------------------

select requester_id as id , count(requester_id) as num
from (select requester_id from RequestAccepted 
union all
select accepter_id from RequestAccepted) as temp
group by id
order by num desc limit 1 ;

